{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_fitb26pknlm76vibeatx77d272ff4ufbeyh5xw7imphvgbnsekzq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now implement compiler.rs functions. The `compile_file` calls things from compiler module, but we need to use the lex_process module's lex / lex_process_create internally. The tricky part: these are in different namespaces. The compiler::lex function takes &mut compiler::LexProcess which is a different struct from lex_process::LexProcess.\n\nFor compile_file, I can simply call:\n1. `cprocess::compile_process_create` to read the file\n2. Build a `lex_process::LexProcess` and use it\n3. Run `lexer::lex` and `parser::parse`\n\nLet me edit compiler.rs to fill in functions:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3513,"cache_read_input_tokens":97507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3513,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55bdd277-df75-4a48-8790-fb729f543af2","uuid":"4564b973-2ff0-4973-91b8-41be8efa3268"}
